positions.description:
Position: Property Management Specialist (Chinese Language Proficiency)
— Bridge asset value with language and start your career in central Tokyo

We are looking for someone who:
- Language: Can communicate in Chinese at a business level and work smoothly with overseas / Greater China owners;
- Basic skills: Can use Word / Excel and other common office tools;
- Work style: Patient, detail-oriented, good at listening, and able to collaborate effectively;
- Growth mindset: Interested in property management and overseas asset operations (no prior experience required; senior members will mentor you end-to-end).

Work location:
Bourn Mark Ningyocho BLD. 2F, 1-2-12 Nihonbashi Ningyocho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo
▶ Access: 2-minute walk from Ningyocho Station
